# Grappling Kraken {4}{U}{U}, 5/6: "Landfall -- Whenever a land you control enters, tap target creature an opponent controls and put a stun counter on it"
# (CR 603.2, 122.1d, 701.26a). Bot2's own land on turn 2 is no land Bot1 controls, so it triggers nothing and its Memnite stays untapped. Bot1's
# Island on turn 3 refuses Bot1's own Ornithopter and Kraken: Bot2's Memnite is tapped and stunned. Bot2's untap step on turn 4 removes the
# counter instead of untapping it, so it is still tapped when Bot1's second Island on turn 5 targets it again (the ruling: an already tapped
# creature may be targeted): it only gets a stun counter, and Bot2's untap step on turn 6 spends that one in turn.

